cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "emu_pk: a differentiable linear matter power spectrum emulator"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the works it builds on."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Comparat
    given-names: Johan
    email: jcomparat@lpsc.in2p3.fr
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9200-1497"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JohanComparat/emu_pk"
url: "https://emu-pk.readthedocs.io/en/stable/"
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-31"
abstract: >-
  emu_pk emulates the linear matter power spectrum over an eight-parameter
  cosmology, including the summed neutrino mass and CPL dark energy, to
  k = 200 h/Mpc and z = 5. It is written in JAX and is differentiable, so
  derivatives with respect to cosmological parameters come from automatic
  differentiation rather than finite differences. Two of those derivatives are
  exact by construction, because the primordial power law is divided out of the
  training target and restored analytically.
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      CosmoPower: emulating cosmological power spectra for accelerated Bayesian
      inference from next-generation surveys
    authors:
      - family-names: "Spurio Mancini"
        given-names: A.
      - family-names: Piras
        given-names: D.
      - family-names: Alsing
        given-names: J.
      - family-names: Joachimi
        given-names: B.
      - family-names: Hobson
        given-names: M. P.
    journal: "Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society"
    volume: 511
    issue: 2
    start: 1771
    end: 1788
    year: 2022
    doi: 10.1093/mnras/stac064
    notes: >-
      The network architecture and the learned activation are theirs; emu_pk
      reproduces both and differs in the training box, the wavenumber reach and
      the training target.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      The Cosmic Linear Anisotropy Solving System (CLASS). Part II:
      Approximation schemes
    authors:
      - family-names: Blas
        given-names: Diego
      - family-names: Lesgourgues
        given-names: Julien
      - family-names: Tram
        given-names: Thomas
    journal: "Journal of Cosmology and Astroparticle Physics"
    volume: 2011
    issue: 07
    start: 034
    year: 2011
    doi: 10.1088/1475-7516/2011/07/034
    notes: "Every training spectrum and every validation reference is a CLASS solve."
  - type: article
    title: >-
      CSST cosmological emulator I: Matter power spectrum emulation with one
      percent accuracy to k = 10 h/Mpc
    authors:
      - family-names: Chen
        given-names: Zhao
      - family-names: Yu
        given-names: Yu
      - family-names: Han
        given-names: Jiaxin
      - family-names: Jing
        given-names: Yipeng
    journal: "Science China Physics, Mechanics, and Astronomy"
    volume: 68
    issue: 8
    start: 289512
    year: 2025
    doi: 10.1007/s11433-025-2671-0
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.11160"
    notes: >-
      The CSST matter power spectrum emulator, cited as the closest comparable
      work rather than a dependency: emu_pk emulates the *linear* spectrum and
